@lang pt
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cp-dominio`
IMPORT `cp-pena`

-- Código Penal, Títulos VIII e IX (arts. 250–288-A) — what the g4b modules
-- share. Nouns, and the few rules every offence in the range reads the same
-- way. No article is encoded here: each article lives in the module of its
-- Capítulo. Written by g4b.
--
-- WHY A SHARED CASE HEADER. Almost every offence in this range has an
-- intentional and a culpable form (art. 18), may be attempted (art. 14), and
-- is qualified by a death or an injury that follows it (arts. 258, 263, 264,
-- 267, 285). Those facts are the same for every article, so they are one
-- record, `Dados comuns do fato`, which each article's case record embeds;
-- what only one article names stays on that article's record.
--
-- Two nouns here are proposed for `cp-dominio.l4` (PROPOSTO-COMUM, listed in
-- notes/g4b.md): `Elemento subjetivo` and `Profissão de saúde`.

§ `Títulos VIII e IX — o que os módulos do grupo g4b compartilham`

§§ `Elemento subjetivo (art. 18)`

-- "Art. 18 - Diz-se o crime: I - doloso, quando o agente quis o resultado ou
-- assumiu o risco de produzi-lo; II - culposo, quando o agente deu causa ao
-- resultado por imprudência, negligência ou imperícia." (art. 18, g1a's)
-- "Parágrafo único - Salvo os casos expressos em lei, ninguém pode ser punido
-- por fato previsto como crime, senão quando o pratica dolosamente."
-- So every offence below is intentional only, unless its own article states a
-- culpable form ("Se culposo o incêndio", "No caso de culpa", "Se o crime é
-- culposo"); a culpable fact under an article with no such form is no crime.
-- Which of the two a fact was is a finding of fact, supplied as input.
-- PROPOSTO-COMUM: every Título with a culpable form needs it (arts. 121 § 3º,
-- 129 § 6º, 180 § 3º, 250–285, 312 § 2º, 351 § 4º ...), and art. 18 is g1a's.
-- `Elemento subjetivo` (dolo, culpa) is declared in cp-dominio.l4 (integration, 2026-09-30).

§§ `A imputação do resultado mais grave (art. 19)`

-- "Art. 19 - Pelo resultado que agrava especialmente a pena, só responde o
-- agente que o houver causado ao menos culposamente." (g1a's article)
-- The death or injury itself is recorded in the shared `Fato`'s `resultados`;
-- this says how it stands to the agent. The second member is fork F-g4b-02:
-- a death or injury the agent WANTED (or whose risk he took on) is not the
-- "resultado" that arts. 258, 264 and 267 qualify a crime of danger with — it
-- is a homicide or an intentional injury (arts. 121, 129), another crime —
-- so those articles' increases do not reach it.
-- Renamed from `Imputação do resultado` (integration, 2026-09-30): g1a's type of that name
-- is art. 13's causation outcome, a different concept.
DECLARE `Imputação do resultado agravador (art. 19)` IS ONE OF
    `causado ao menos culposamente, sem ser querido`
    @nlg:en caused by the agent at least through fault, without the agent wanting it or taking on its risk
    `querido ou assumido pelo agente`
    @nlg:en wanted by the agent, or its risk taken on (intent as to the result)
    `não causado pelo agente sequer culposamente`
    @nlg:en not caused by the agent even through fault (art. 19 bars it)

§§ `O perigo (arts. 250 a 256)`

-- "expondo a perigo a vida, a integridade física ou o patrimônio de outrem"
-- (arts. 250, 251, 252, 254, 255, 256). "de outrem": a danger only to the
-- agent himself or his own property is not it.
DECLARE `Bem exposto a perigo` IS ONE OF
    `a vida de outrem`
    @nlg:en the life of another
    `a integridade física de outrem`
    @nlg:en the bodily integrity of another
    `o patrimônio de outrem`
    @nlg:en the property of another

-- The danger the act created. Capítulo I is headed "DOS CRIMES DE PERIGO
-- COMUM": read with it, the danger must threaten people or goods in an
-- indeterminate number, not one determinate person (fork F-g4b-01). Whether it
-- did is the fact supplier's finding.
DECLARE `Perigo criado` HAS
    `bens expostos a perigo` IS A LIST OF `Bem exposto a perigo`
    @nlg:en what the act put in danger
    `perigo comum, a número indeterminado de pessoas ou bens` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the danger threatened an indeterminate number of people or goods, not one determinate person

@ref CP arts. 250, 251, 252, 254, 255 e 256 — "expondo a perigo a vida, a integridade física ou o patrimônio de outrem"; Capítulo I, "DOS CRIMES DE PERIGO COMUM"
GIVEN p IS A `Perigo criado`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the act exposed the life, bodily integrity or property of others to a common danger
`expondo a perigo a vida, a integridade física ou o patrimônio de outrem` p MEANS
        NOT null (p's `bens expostos a perigo`)
    AND "perigo comum" ... p's `perigo comum, a número indeterminado de pessoas ou bens`

§§ `O que o agente fez`

-- The verbs the Código uses in this range, one member each. Every article
-- reads the list for its own verbs; a verb it does not name does not make
-- its crime. "de qualquer forma, distribui ou entrega a consumo" (arts.
-- 272 § 1º-A, 273 § 1º, 276, 278): "de qualquer forma" widens HOW, so it is
-- in the member's gloss and not a member of its own.
DECLARE `Ação do agente` IS ONE OF
    fabricar
    @nlg:en to manufacture
    fornecer
    @nlg:en to supply
    adquirir
    @nlg:en to acquire
    possuir
    @nlg:en to possess
    transportar
    @nlg:en to transport
    remover
    @nlg:en to remove
    destruir
    @nlg:en to destroy
    inutilizar
    @nlg:en to render useless
    subtrair
    @nlg:en to take away
    ocultar
    @nlg:en to hide
    impedir
    @nlg:en to prevent
    dificultar
    @nlg:en to hinder
    perturbar
    @nlg:en to disturb
    interromper
    @nlg:en to interrupt
    envenenar
    @nlg:en to poison
    corromper
    @nlg:en to corrupt
    poluir
    @nlg:en to pollute
    adulterar
    @nlg:en to adulterate
    falsificar
    @nlg:en to falsify
    alterar
    @nlg:en to alter
    importar
    @nlg:en to import
    vender
    @nlg:en to sell
    `expor à venda`
    @nlg:en to expose for sale
    `ter em depósito para vender`
    @nlg:en to hold in stock in order to sell
    `ter em depósito para distribuir`
    @nlg:en to hold in stock so that it be distributed
    `ter em depósito`
    @nlg:en to hold in stock
    distribuir
    @nlg:en to distribute, in any way
    `entregar a consumo`
    @nlg:en to deliver for consumption, in any way
    ceder
    @nlg:en to hand over

§§ `Profissões de saúde (arts. 268, 269, 282)`

-- The professions the Código names in this range. PROPOSTO-COMUM: art. 128
-- ("praticado por médico"), art. 302 ("Dar o médico ... atestado falso") and
-- others outside this range name them too.
DECLARE `Profissão de saúde` IS ONE OF
    médico
    @nlg:en a physician
    `médico veterinário`
    @nlg:en a veterinarian
    dentista
    @nlg:en a dentist
    farmacêutico
    @nlg:en a pharmacist
    enfermeiro
    @nlg:en a nurse

§§ `Dados comuns do fato`

-- The part of a case every offence in the range reads the same way. Each
-- article's case record embeds one of these as `comum`.
--   * `execução iniciada` and `consumação impedida ...` are the facts art. 14,
--     II reads; whether the crime was consummated is never supplied: it is
--     computed from the article's elements (art. 14, I).
--   * `imputação do resultado` matters only where `fato`'s `resultados` is
--     not empty.
DECLARE `Dados comuns do fato` HAS
    agente IS AN Agente
    @nlg:en the agent
    fato IS A Fato
    @nlg:en the act: its date, the people who took part, the means, the results and the circumstances
    `elemento subjetivo` IS AN `Elemento subjetivo`
    @nlg:en whether the agent acted with intent or through fault
    `imputação do resultado` IS AN `Imputação do resultado agravador (art. 19)`
    @nlg:en how a death or injury that followed the act stands to the agent
    `execução iniciada` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the agent began to carry out the act
    `consumação impedida por circunstâncias alheias à vontade do agente` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en something outside the agent's will stopped the act from being completed

-- A death or injury that followed the act, and reaches the agent as the
-- qualifying result of a crime of danger: it occurred, he caused it at least
-- through fault (art. 19), and he did not want it (fork F-g4b-02).
@ref CP art. 19
GIVEN dc IS A `Dados comuns do fato`
      r  IS A Resultado
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the result followed the act and is imputed to the agent as the qualifying result
`o resultado é imputável ao agente (art. 19)` dc r MEANS
        elem r (dc's fato's resultados)
    AND dc's `imputação do resultado` EQUALS `causado ao menos culposamente, sem ser querido`

@ref CP art. 18, I
GIVEN dc IS A `Dados comuns do fato`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the agent acted with intent
`doloso (art. 18, I)` dc MEANS dc's `elemento subjetivo` EQUALS dolo

@ref CP art. 18, II
GIVEN dc IS A `Dados comuns do fato`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the agent acted through fault
`culposo (art. 18, II)` dc MEANS dc's `elemento subjetivo` EQUALS culpa

-- The intentional crime, consummated: intent, and every element present.
-- A culpable fact is never an attempt (art. 14, II needs a will that
-- something outside it thwarted).
@ref CP art. 14, I; art. 18, I
GIVEN dc IS A `Dados comuns do fato`
      `os elementos do tipo estão reunidos` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the intentional crime is consummated
`o crime doloso está consumado` dc `os elementos do tipo estão reunidos` MEANS
        `doloso (art. 18, I)` dc
    AND `crime consumado (art. 14, I)` `os elementos do tipo estão reunidos`

@ref CP art. 14, II; art. 18, I
GIVEN dc IS A `Dados comuns do fato`
      `os elementos do tipo estão reunidos` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the intentional crime is attempted
`o crime doloso está tentado` dc `os elementos do tipo estão reunidos` MEANS
        `doloso (art. 18, I)` dc
    AND `crime tentado (art. 14, II)` (dc's `execução iniciada`) `os elementos do tipo estão reunidos` (dc's `consumação impedida por circunstâncias alheias à vontade do agente`)

-- The culpable crime, where the article states one: fault, and every element.
@ref CP art. 18, II e parágrafo único
GIVEN dc IS A `Dados comuns do fato`
      `os elementos do tipo estão reunidos` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the crime committed through fault is made out
`o crime culposo está configurado` dc `os elementos do tipo estão reunidos` MEANS
        `culposo (art. 18, II)` dc
    AND `os elementos do tipo estão reunidos`

-- The attempt's reduction, added to a list of causes when the crime was
-- attempted (art. 14, parágrafo único).
@ref CP art. 14, parágrafo único
GIVEN tentado IS A BOOLEAN
      causas IS A LIST OF `Causa de aumento ou de diminuição`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Causa de aumento ou de diminuição`
@nlg:en the causes, with the attempt's reduction added if the crime was attempted
`as causas, com a da tentativa se tentado` tentado causas MEANS
    IF   tentado
    THEN append causas (LIST `diminuição pela tentativa (art. 14, parágrafo único)`)
    ELSE causas

-- A cause joins the list only where it applies.
GIVEN incide IS A BOOLEAN
      c      IS A `Causa de aumento ou de diminuição`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Causa de aumento ou de diminuição`
@nlg:en the cause, if it applies
`a causa em lista, se incide` incide c MEANS
    IF incide THEN LIST c ELSE EMPTY

§§ `O conhecimento da qualidade da coisa negociada (arts. 253, 270 a 278)`

-- Art. 18, parágrafo único: a crime is punishable only with dolo unless the law
-- says otherwise, and an error about an element excludes dolo (art. 20). For a
-- crime of dealing in, holding, supplying or carrying a thing that has a
-- quality (poisoned, adulterated, harmful, explosive), knowing the quality is
-- part of the dolo. `Elemento subjetivo` has only dolo and culpa, so a dealer
-- who took the thing for sound, with no negligence at all, could be recorded
-- only as culpa, and the culpable forms (arts. 270 § 2º, 272 § 2º, 273 § 2º,
-- 278 parágrafo único) would convict him. This finding states the third case,
-- and it means no crime (fork F-g4b-29). Not knowing that the law forbids the
-- dealing is art. 21's and is not stated here.
DECLARE `Conhecimento da qualidade da coisa negociada` IS ONE OF
    `sabia da qualidade da coisa negociada`
    @nlg:en the agent knew what the thing was: poisoned, falsified, harmful, explosive or the like
    `ignorava a qualidade da coisa negociada, por culpa`
    @nlg:en the agent did not know what the thing was, and would have known with the care the circumstances asked of him
    `ignorava a qualidade da coisa negociada, sem culpa`
    @nlg:en the agent did not know what the thing was, and could not have known with the care the circumstances asked of him

-- The dolo of a dealing verb needs the knowledge. An agent who made the
-- quality himself (poisoned, adulterated, manufactured) knows it, and needs no
-- separate finding: `produziu` is TRUE for him.
@ref CP art. 18, parágrafo único; art. 20
GIVEN produziu IS A BOOLEAN
      conhecimento IS A `Conhecimento da qualidade da coisa negociada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the agent made the quality of the thing himself, or knew it
`a ciência da qualidade basta ao dolo` produziu conhecimento MEANS
        produziu
    OR  conhecimento EQUALS `sabia da qualidade da coisa negociada`

-- The culpable form of a dealing verb: the agent did not know, and his not
-- knowing is itself a want of care. One who made the quality himself is judged
-- on the making, not on a knowledge he does not lack.
@ref CP art. 18, II e parágrafo único; art. 20, caput, segunda parte
GIVEN produziu IS A BOOLEAN
      conhecimento IS A `Conhecimento da qualidade da coisa negociada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the agent made the quality of the thing himself, or did not know it through want of care
`o desconhecimento da qualidade é culposo` produziu conhecimento MEANS
        produziu
    OR  conhecimento EQUALS `ignorava a qualidade da coisa negociada, por culpa`
